<title>USA: Curtiss-Wright stake cut by Gabelli group.</title>
<headline>Curtiss-Wright stake cut by Gabelli group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investment manager Mario Gabelli said Friday it cut its stake in Curtiss-Wright Corp to 570,320 common shares or 11.21 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 26,400 common shares sold between June 27 and August 7 at prices ranging from $60.0208 and $70.7417 per share.</p>
<p>Curtiss-Wright, based in Lyndhurst, N.J., deals in aviation equipment.</p>
</text>
